        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add glossary page for "registrable domain" instead of "eTLD"]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42588</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42588"/>
        <updated>2026-01-01T00:42:19.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">I'd like to link to a glossary definition of "registrable domain" <a href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42338" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/42338/hovercard">in the passkeys guide</a>. It turns out that although we don't have one, we do have a page for eTLD.</p>
<p dir="auto">But I think "registrable domain" is a better glossary entry, for three reasons:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>"registrable domain" is the <a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#host-registrable-domain" rel="nofollow">spec term</a>. The spec doesn't talk about eTLD AFAICT.</li>
<li>"registrable domain" is more comprehensible</li>
<li>we never actually link to "eTLD" we only link to "eTLD+1", which is the same as registrable domain. So we currently have to link into a fragment of the glossary entry, rather than directly to it.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
